==Latin==

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*peth₂-}}
From {{der|la|ine-pro|*péth₂eti||to fall; fly}}. Cognates include {{cog|grc|πέτομαι||I fly}}, {{cog|sa|पतति|tr=pátati|sc=Deva}}, {{cog|ae|𐬞𐬀𐬙𐬀𐬌𐬙𐬌|tr=pataiti}} and {{cog|xcl|թիռ||flight, desire}}. See English {{m|en|feather}}, {{m|en|pen}} for more.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|petō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3.poet-sync-perf|petō|petīv/peti|petīt}}

# I [[ask]], [[beg]], [[request]].
# I [[make for]] (somewhere).
# I [[seek]], [[aim]] at, [[desire]].
#: ''Auxilium deorum '''peto'''.''
#:: '''I am seeking''' the help of the gods.
#: ''Altiora '''peto'''.''
#:: '''I seek''' higher things.
# I [[beg]], [[beseech]]
## I [[beg]] of/from someone ({{m|la|ab}} + ''ablative'') for something (+ ''accusative'' or a clause with ''ut'' or ''ne'')
# I [[attack]], I [[assail]], I [[thrust]] at
#: '''''Petere''' aliquem hasta.''
#:: To '''attack''' someone with a spear.
# I [[aim]] at {{gloss|with the person attacked in the ''accusative'' and the weapon/projectile in the ''ablative''}}
# {{lb|la|ecclesiastical}} To [[missionize]] or [[proselytize]] among the people of a place.
#: ''Peter Romam Marcus Alexandriam '''petit'''''.
#:: Peter proselytizes in Rome; Mark, in Alexandria. (Bede, ''Chronica Minor'')

